Summary of modifications
------------------------
The upstream project provides the Jupyter-kernel execution environment, the
dataset server, and the benchmark agent. Work added in this fork:

  * Trajectory forking (scripts/fork/) -- rewinding a graded agent run to the
    earliest step a judge marked wrong, injecting that judge's feedback, and
    re-rolling from there, plus the all-feedback ablation arm and the tooling to
    inspect and re-grade the results.
  * A pluggable judge framework (src/hypotest/env/judges/) covering BixBench,
    BioMysteryBench, HeurekaBench, BiomniBench-DA and bioagent-bench, including
    deterministic (non-LLM) grading and the per-criterion first-wrong-step
    derivation that forking depends on.
  * Benchmark dataset converters and capsule staging (scripts/data/).
  * A hypothesis-proposer subsystem (proposer/).
  * An RL/GRPO training stack (rl/) -- incomplete; see README.md.
  * Substantial changes to the execution environment itself, including image
    stripping, an idle-environment sweeper, configurable notebook output limits
    and prompt revisions.

Individual modifications are recorded in docs/patches.md, and modified files
carry "PATCH N" markers referring to it.
